    "pairs": "All unordered pairs of noninitial working controls; one is identified with the other. The initial state is excluded.",
    "actions": "Both replacement rows are synthesized. Write 0/1, move L/R, and target a surviving working control. No new control and no direct halt target are synthesized. All incoming targets of the removed state are redirected.",
    "simulation": "Each original one-step effect must be matched in 1..120 steps of the final edited table, on every supplied local context. Head position, entire window contents, and successor after identification agree. Intermediate visits to the merged control use the same synthesized rows. Leaving the window or exceeding fuel rejects that local simulation.",
    "windows": "Radius K is the centered interval [-K,K]. Abstract transitions permit either newly entering boundary bit. All-tape and blank modes differ at their initial window sets. Source mode narrows only supplied non-box controls and includes every exact bootstrap window, including the endpoint.",
    "limitations": "No lower bound for arbitrary consistency Turing machines. Excludes initial-state identifications, larger quotients, additional edits elsewhere, new helper states, halt-target synthesis, longer detours, and different simulation relations. An overapproximation can reject a valid reduction outside this sufficient local criterion."
